From: rcllf local patch
Subject: [PATCH] socket_common: retry accept() on timeout instead of giving up

accept_socket() tested `errno != EAGAIN || errno != EWOULDBLOCK || errno != EINTR`,
which is always true. The listening socket carries a 10 s SO_RCVTIMEO, so the
first accept() timeout (EAGAIN) ended the loop and the RTI stopped waiting for
federates that had not connected yet ("RTI failed to accept the federate.").

Backport of the hunk upstream reactor-c already carries on main (commit
8bcc07061, merged with lf-lang/reactor-c PR #358, 2026-08-14), applied to the
pinned submodule 2f63540d4. Drop this patch when the pin moves past 564b622d1.
---
--- a/network/impl/src/socket_common.c
+++ b/network/impl/src/socket_common.c
@@ -201,8 +201,11 @@
     if (socket_id >= 0) {
       // Got a socket
       break;
-    } else if (socket_id < 0 && (errno != EAGAIN || errno != EWOULDBLOCK || errno != EINTR)) {
-      if (errno != ECONNABORTED) {
+    } else if (socket_id < 0 && (errno != EAGAIN && errno != EWOULDBLOCK && errno != EINTR)) {
+      // ECONNABORTED: a connection was aborted before accept() could complete — not fatal.
+      // EINVAL: the socket was shut down (e.g., shutdown_socket() was called to unblock this
+      // accept() intentionally when the RTI is shutting down) — expected, not an error.
+      if (errno != ECONNABORTED && errno != EINVAL) {
         lf_print_warning("Failed to accept the socket. %s.", strerror(errno));
       }
       break;
